# Nirvana project: environment reference (.env.example)
# `nrv init` creates no .env. Create one only for what you need below; its
# variables reach every dispatch from this project. Not set here:
#   - the project's scope: `scope` in .nirvana/project.yaml
#     (`nrv init --scope=<global|project|merge>`)
#   - engine settings (performance profile, effort, context ceiling, review,
#     routing): `nrv config list` / `nrv config set <key> <value>`
#   - a squad's credentials: declared in its dependencies.yaml; `nrv doctor`
#     lists the missing ones

# --- Scope filters (merge scope only) ---------------------------------------
# Limit which global entries are visible (comma-separated slugs):
# NIRVANA_GLOBAL_INCLUDE_ONLY=brandcraft,copy-lab
# NIRVANA_GLOBAL_EXCLUDE=old-squad

# --- Paths (each defaults under $HOME) --------------------------------------
# NIRVANA_HOME=$HOME
# SQUADS_DIR=$HOME/squads
# BUSINESSES_DIR=$HOME/businesses
# HARNESS_LOGS_DIR=$HOME/.harness-logs

# --- Runtime cascade (opt-in) -----------------------------------------------
# When a runtime hits its plan limit (5-hour window, weekly cap, quota), the
# dispatch hands the run to the next runtime in the list and records
# runtime_handoff in the audit. Without it, one runtime and no fallback.
# Syntax per entry: runtime[:model][@provider][$budget_usd]
# LLM_CASCADE=claude-code,codex,antigravity-cli
# LLM_CASCADE=claude-code:opus,claude-code:sonnet,codex:gpt-5.5$10
# NIRVANA_COOLDOWN_FILE=<project>/.nirvana/state/runtime-cooldowns.json

# --- Runtime rules: which runtime runs which kind of work -------------------
# In plain language. A flag (--runtime) or a runtime named in the request wins
# over these; NOT_USE_<runtime> vetoes a runtime for matching requests.
# USE_CLAUDE_CODE="Long writing, code and the general default"
# USE_CODEX="Image generation and visual refinement"
# USE_GEMINI="Huge context (1M tokens)"
# NOT_USE_GEMINI="Codebase analysis"
# Also: USE_ANTIGRAVITY, USE_KIMI, USE_GROK, USE_PI, USE_HERMES.

# --- Authentication ----------------------------------------------------------
# Each runtime signs in through its own CLI, once. Claude Code uses the
# account's OAuth; set a token only if you prefer an explicit one:
# CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN=
